[{:adr/consequences "{:single_fix_point \"a recipe fix (ComfyUI error-handling edge case, parse-structured fence-stripping bug, etc.) now lands once in genapp-clj and reaches both apps instead of drifting between hand-copied files\", :third_app_ready \"a third LangGraph generation app in this style (animeka's own CLAUDE.md references 'shared with mangaka and dogaka' for the kami-cine bridge, implying prior art for at least one more sibling) starts from genapp-clj + a config map instead of copy-pasting a third time\", :new_dependency_edge \"both apps now depend on kotoba-lang/genapp-clj in addition to their existing com-junkawasaki/{langgraph,comfyui,langchain}-clj pins -- consistent with repos.edn's stated org-migration direction (com-junkawasaki generic -clj libs migrating out to kotoba-lang; this lands directly in kotoba-lang rather than com-junkawasaki first)\", :store_duplication_remains \"store.cljc's ~90%-different schema duplication is deliberately unaddressed -- it encodes each app's actual domain, not shared infrastructure\"}", :adr/correction "{:what_was_wrong [\"bundled 4 unrelated-enough concerns into one repo: blob+checkpoint (truly domain-agnostic LangGraph storage primitives) vs comfy+llm (specific-tool JVM I/O adapters for comfyui-clj/langchain-clj's pure cores)\" \"\\\"genapp\\\" is an invented, non-standard name with no clear referent\" \"built on the STALE org: kotoba-lang/comfyui and kotoba-lang/langchain already existed as the migrated successors of com-junkawasaki/comfyui-clj and com-junkawasaki/langchain-clj (kotoba-lang/langgraph's tip commit literally reads \\\"chore(reconcile): org-rename -> kotoba-lang\\\"; kotoba-lang/comfyui's tip SHA 2a653b1 was byte-identical to what genapp-clj had just pinned from com-junkawasaki/comfyui-clj) -- genapp-clj was accidentally built one repo away from its own natural home\"], :dep_hygiene \"comfyui.gateway's and langchain.jvm's http-kit/jsonista deps live ONLY in each repo's :test alias, not main :deps -- langchain's deps.edn documents a 'zero third-party runtime dependencies by design' invariant (every ns .cljc, runs on JVM/CLJS/SCI/WASM) that unconditional http-kit would have broken for non-JVM consumers; every actual consumer (mangaka/animeka/shiropico) already declares http-kit/jsonista itself\", :date \"2026-07-01\", :migration_completed_for_consumers \"mangaka/animeka/shiropico's deps.edn now point langgraph/comfyui/langchain at kotoba-lang, not com-junkawasaki -- completing the migration repos.edn's :orgs taxonomy note already declared as the direction. Also fixed the same off-by-2-levels :dev :local/root path bug (5 levels up instead of 3) for the kotoba-lang targets.\", :compatibility_check \"diff'd every file genapp.comfy/genapp.llm actually required (comfyui.{node,std,queue,exec}, langchain.{model,message,db,kotoba_db}) between com-junkawasaki and kotoba-lang copies before touching anything -- all byte-identical except langgraph.checkpoint (kotoba-lang added a backward-compatible :db/id field); ran genapp-clj's own test suite against kotoba-lang-sourced deps first, separating 'safe to swap orgs' from 'split the bundle'\", :manifest \"repos.edn/west.yml updated via the same GitHub API single-entry method as ADR-2607011816 (genapp-clj entry removed, langgraph-store added, comfyui/langchain/mangaka/animeka/shiropico pins advanced) -- same rationale (shallow-clone false-positive risk, concurrent fleet checkouts of these exact shared kotoba-lang repos, one of which (langchain) was confirmed to have another agent's WIP branch checked out in a separate worktree at the time)\", :deletion \"kotoba-lang/genapp-clj deleted (gh repo delete) once all three consumers' facades were repointed and re-verified green: mangaka 82/560, animeka 5/32, shiropico 19/49 -- all unchanged across both the original extraction and this correction, proving the facade pattern absorbs relocation with zero call-site changes\", :split {:comfyui_gateway {:from \"genapp.comfy\", :to \"orgs/kotoba-lang/comfyui, ns comfyui.gateway\", :pr 1, :tests \"9 tests / 26 assertions added, 18/69 repo-wide\"}, :langchain_jvm {:from \"genapp.llm\", :to \"orgs/kotoba-lang/langchain, ns langchain.jvm\", :pr 6, :tests \"8 tests / 20 assertions added\"}, :langgraph_store {:from \"genapp.blob + genapp.checkpoint\", :to \"orgs/kotoba-lang/langgraph-store (new repo, no -clj suffix per kotoba-lang naming convention)\", :tests \"8 tests / 19 assertions (blob 3, checkpoint 5 -- checkpoint had no direct unit tests in genapp-clj, added fresh)\"}}, :trigger \"direct user feedback on genapp-clj immediately after it shipped: 'comfy, llm は別で分けた方がいいかな. genapp は一般的ではないので、一般的な名前にできる?' (should comfy/llm be split out separately? genapp isn't a generic-enough name, can it be made more generic?)\"}", :adr/authoritative_for ["CORRECTION (same day): kotoba-lang/genapp-clj was split apart and DELETED. comfy -> comfyui.gateway (orgs/kotoba-lang/comfyui), llm -> langchain.jvm (orgs/kotoba-lang/langchain), blob+checkpoint -> orgs/kotoba-lang/langgraph-store (no -clj suffix). See :correction below -- this is the current, authoritative shape." "store.cljc (the durable domain schema) is NOT extracted -- mangaka's page/panel schema and animeka's work/episode/scene/cut schema are genuinely different domains (~90% line-diff measured), matching ADR-2606282100's rejection of forcing per-work data into a generic shape" "new generic libraries land in kotoba-lang directly, not com-junkawasaki first, per repos.edn's own stated org-migration direction -- AND kotoba-lang repos do not use the -clj suffix com-junkawasaki's langgraph-clj/comfyui-clj/langchain-clj use (langgraph-store, not langgraph-store-clj)" "a shared generic library must not be named after one consumer -- the same naming correction already made once in ADR-2607011816 (animeka, not mangaka, as SHIRO & PICO's consumer) -- AND must not be named for an artificial bundling concern (\"genapp\") when its parts belong split to their pure-engine siblings' own repos"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "genapp-clj-commons-extraction", :adr/related ["CLAUDE.md" "90-docs/adr/2606282100-mangaka-render-commons-vs-sip-work-split.md" "90-docs/adr/2607011816-ghosthacker-shiropico-standalone-repo.md" "manifest/repos.edn" "orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-mangaka PR #1+#2" "orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-animeka PR #1+#2" "orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico PR #3" "orgs/kotoba-lang/comfyui PR #1 (feat/gateway-jvm-adapter)" "orgs/kotoba-lang/langchain PR #6 (feat/jvm-host-adapter)" "orgs/kotoba-lang/langgraph-store (new repo)"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607011900-genapp-clj-mangaka-animeka-commons", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-01", :adr/decision "{:new_repo {:path \"orgs/kotoba-lang/genapp-clj\", :remote \"kotoba-lang\", :visibility :private, :namespaces {:genapp.blob \"content-addressed blob store, ported verbatim (byte-identical originals)\", :genapp.checkpoint \"latest-only LangGraph checkpointer over langchain.db, ported verbatim (byte-identical originals)\", :genapp.comfy \"ComfyUI txt2img rendering, config-driven: :node-type/:default-ckpt/:default-width/:default-height/:require-api-key?/env-var-name-lists/:placeholder -- dependency inversion, same pattern as kami-mangaka-render-clj's :mappers (ADR-2606282100)\", :genapp.llm \"ChatModel offline-mock fallback + JSON/EDN structured-output parsing + vision message-building; model provider stays app-specific, injected as a build-live thunk\"}, :not_extracted {:runtime.cljc \"thin glue wiring an app-specific store to blob/checkpoint, too small/coupled to be worth its own facade\", :store.cljc \"genuinely domain-specific (page/panel vs work/episode/scene/cut schema, ~90% line-diff) -- forcing one schema would repeat the anti-pattern ADR-2606282100 already rejected for render_anchors.edn-style per-work data\"}, :head_sha \"69abd6bcc50fd05a3c4e28d9730fc2b30e9cc19a\"}, :facade_pattern \"each app keeps its original 4 namespaces (mangaka.blob, mangaka.comfy, etc.) as thin facades over genapp.* preserving exact original public function names/arities -- no call-site changes anywhere else in either app, same shape sip.render used as a facade over kami.mangaka.render in ADR-2606282100\", :consumer_repos {:ai_gftd_mangaka {:pr 1, :branch \"refactor/extract-genapp-clj\", :head_sha \"14300a49c7bef013f7caaebcedb5fbdd8a50c1d0\", :tests \"82 tests / 560 assertions, 0 failures/errors (unchanged from pre-refactor)\"}, :ai_gftd_animeka {:pr 1, :branch \"refactor/extract-genapp-clj\", :head_sha \"2fe8b0fc68619600c9d6adf3c35f193d5eb40b19\", :tests \"5 tests / 32 assertions, 0 failures/errors (unchanged from pre-refactor)\"}}, :manifest_registration {:repos_edn \"added \\\"orgs/kotoba-lang/genapp-clj\\\" to :extra-projects via GitHub Contents API single-entry commit (blob-sha-matched PUT against origin/main tip)\", :west_yml \"added one project entry (alphabetically between fs and godaddy-dns, matching gen-west-manifest.cljs's sorted output) plus advanced ai-gftd-mangaka's and ai-gftd-animeka's pins to their new post-refactor HEADs, all via the same API method\", :why_api_not_local \"same rationale as ADR-2607011816: local superproject checkout state is unreliable this session (shallow-clone false-positive '(forced update)' warnings, verified harmless each time via gh api compare per CLAUDE.md's newly-documented check; concurrent fleet writers touching the same shared checkout)\"}}", :db/id -1, :adr/problem "{:source \"user request 2026-07-01: '1, 2, 3' -- proceed with (1) extracting the mangaka/animeka shared runtime layer, (2) placing it under kotoba-lang with a neutral name, (3) evaluating an actor wrapper for animeka -- after a prior exploratory turn measured real duplication and confirmed langgraph-clj/comfyui-clj/langchain-clj were already shared but the layer built on top of them was not\", :investigated [\"ai-gftd-animeka's own deps.edn states 'Pins mirror mangaka' and its CLAUDE.md self-describes as mangaka's anime sibling; file-by-file diff (name-normalized) of the 9 identically-named files confirmed real duplication, not just shared upstream deps: blob.cljc/checkpoint.cljc byte-identical (25/22 diff lines out of ~60/40), comfy.cljc/llm.cljc same shape with config/provider differences (120/107 diff lines out of ~164/100), store.cljc genuinely domain-specific (532 diff lines out of ~321/270, ~90%)\" \"langgraph-clj/comfyui-clj/langchain-clj were already shared (identical pinned git SHAs in both deps.edn) before this change -- the actual gap was the app-scaffolding layer built on top of them (blob store / checkpointer / comfy gateway client / llm chat-model wiring), not the graph runtime itself\" \"ADR-2606282100 already solved the same shape of problem one layer down (2D-panel-generation inside kami-engine, kami-mangaka-render-clj extracted from sip.render via :mappers dependency injection) -- reused that exact pattern here for genapp.comfy's config and genapp.llm's build-live thunk\" \"mangaka's cljs Studio UI (mangaka.cljs.app / mangaka.cljc.api) does not transitively require any of blob/checkpoint/comfy/llm (pure browser fetch client against /xrpc/*) -- confirmed the refactor has zero cljs build impact before touching those 4 files\" \"both apps' :dev alias :local/root override paths were wrong (5 levels up, should be 3) for this monorepo's actual orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-{mangaka,animeka}/clj/ nesting -- a pre-existing bug that silently made :dev fall back to git-fetching pinned deps; fixed as a drive-by so this refactor could actually be tested locally\"], :risk \"extracting comfy.cljc/llm.cljc (not byte-identical, real config differences) risked silently changing behavior for one app while generalizing for the other -- mitigated by making :require-api-key? and env-var-list config explicit injected parameters (preserving each app's exact original branch, not picking one as 'the' behavior) and running both apps' full existing test suites unchanged after the refactor as the correctness gate, plus adding explicit genapp-level tests for both :require-api-key? branches since that distinction wasn't a branch in either original file alone\"}", :adr/alternatives "[{:option \"leave the duplication (status quo)\", :rejected_because \"the two files were already provably diverging in small ways (mangaka gained vision-score/vision-json, animeka gained env-var fallback chains) that a future bug-fix would have to remember to port twice, or silently wouldn't\"} {:option \"merge store.cljc too, with a generic schema\", :rejected_because \"the two domains (page/panel vs work/episode/scene/cut) are not the same shape; forcing one schema would either lose animeka's cut-level fields or bloat mangaka's page schema with unused columns -- matches ADR-2606282100's rejection of generic anchors/compose for the same reason\"} {:option \"put the extraction under com-junkawasaki (matching the two apps' existing -clj deps) instead of kotoba-lang\", :rejected_because \"repos.edn's own :orgs taxonomy states com-junkawasaki's remaining generic -clj libs are mid-migration OUT to kotoba-lang -- not a landing zone for new ones\"} {:option \"name it after one consumer (e.g. kotoba-lang/mangaka-clj)\", :rejected_because \"exactly the naming anti-pattern already fixed twice this session (ADR-2607011816's mangaka->animeka consumer correction, and ADR-2606282100's original kami-mangaka-render-clj naming decision) -- genapp names what it is, not who uses it\"}]", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607011900: genapp-clj -- shared LangGraph generation-app scaffolding for mangaka/animeka"}]